","evidence_strength_rank":3,"organ_id":"mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer run --input fixtures/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/input --out receipts/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"59dcd28ace8ae81785d87e7b223731e8b19065e6ab3af2f8fd113e5477e6321c","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","family":"formal_math_and_proof","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor"},"component_id":"mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.mathematical_strategy_atlas","plain":"Before proving a statement, someone must pick a first approach, and a program can suggest one by scoring each option. This component is given problem descriptions, such as a statement worded 'if and only if', and strategy cards listing clues for and against each approach. It recalculates each score, adding points for matching clues, subtracting points for opposing clues and adding a small capped bonus for matching search words. It outputs the highest-scoring approach as a hypothesis to try before any proof attempt, or a recorded no-match, and rejects a declared choice that disagrees with it.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/mathematical_strategy_atlas.md","sha256":"fe6312f93d36625b72446ee97816b29a8a4a0ff1a3f90d14fc216131ea46f600","text":"# Mathematical Strategy Atlas\n\n> **In plain terms.** Before proving a statement, someone must pick a first approach, and a program can suggest one by scoring each option. This component is given problem descriptions, such as a statement worded 'if and only if', and strategy cards listing clues for and against each approach. It recalculates each score, adding points for matching clues, subtracting points for opposing clues and adding a small capped bonus for matching search words. It outputs the highest-scoring approach as a hypothesis to try before any proof attempt, or a recorded no-match, and rejects a declared choice that disagrees with it.\n\nThe strategy scorer takes public problem features and strategy cards and recomputes a proposed first strategy before premise retrieval or proof execution. The score weights matching triggers, penalizes negative triggers, and adds a capped bonus for retrieval-term matches. The fixture includes an `iff_goal` case selecting `iff_split`; an unmapped case can yield a typed selection miss.\n\nThe validator rejects an unknown strategy, an exposed oracle label, a proof body, and an invalid declared selection. Tests change features or strategy evidence to check that the selection is recomputed. This is a hypothesis from the supplied features and scoring rules, not evidence that the strategy proves the statement or that a model performs well on a benchmark.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root with Python 3.11 or newer, run the fixture through the Python API. The API accepts an explicit acceptance path; the module CLI does not expose that option:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom microcosm_core.organs.mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer import run\nr = run(\"fixtures/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/input\",\n        \".microcosm/component-guides/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/out\",\n        acceptance_out=\".microcosm/component-guides/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/acceptance.json\")\nprint(r[\"status\"])\nPY\n```\n\nThe supplied fixture prints `pass` when its selections and expected negative cases satisfy the validator.\n\n## Verification\n\nTests check recomputation for selected inputs; they do not prove the scorer or a mathematical statement. `make component-replays` runs the exported strategy bundle through the [shared Dafny admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) for agreement among supplied source, input, claim policy and receipt observations. The direct fixture command does not invoke that gate.\n\n## Source and evidence\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer.py) and [fixture inputs](../fixtures/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/input/).\n- [Tests](../tests/test_mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer.py).\n- [Saved example result](../receipts/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/mathematical_strategy_atlas_result.json) (historical, not a fresh run).\n- [Component JSON record](./mathematical_strategy_atlas.json) and [canonical capsule](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/exported_mathematical_strategy_atlas_bundle_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer run --input fixtures/first_wave/mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer/inp